# Binary water-cosolvent mixtures for COSMO-RS relative-solubility screening.
# Format (whitespace-separated):  <label>  <solvent1>  <solvent2>  <x1>  <x2>
# - solvent1 = organic cosolvent, solvent2 = h2o (COSMObase basenames)
# - x1, x2 are MOLE fractions (sum to 1.0)
#
# IMPORTANT: the label encodes the user's VOLUME ratio (v/v, cosolvent:water),
# but x1/x2 are the MOLE fractions after converting v/v -> mole using solvent
# density + molar mass. E.g. ipa-h2o-1-1 = 1:1 by volume = 0.19/0.81 by mole.
# Component basenames (propanol, ethanol, 2-propanol, methanol, propanone,
# acetonitrile, dioxane, thf, h2o) are all in the prior confirmed panel.

# label               solvent1        solvent2   x1(mol)  x2(mol)
prop-h2o-95-5         propanol        h2o        0.8210   0.1790
prop-h2o-98-2         propanol        h2o        0.9221   0.0779
etoh-h2o-9-1          ethanol         h2o        0.7358   0.2642
etoh-h2o-95-5         ethanol         h2o        0.8546   0.1454
etoh-h2o-3-1          ethanol         h2o        0.4814   0.5186
ipa-h2o-9-1           2-propanol      h2o        0.6802   0.3198
ipa-h2o-95-5          2-propanol      h2o        0.8179   0.1821
ipa-h2o-98-2          2-propanol      h2o        0.9205   0.0795
ipa-h2o-1-1           2-propanol      h2o        0.1912   0.8088
meoh-h2o-1-1          methanol        h2o        0.3087   0.6913
meoh-h2o-3-1          methanol        h2o        0.5726   0.4274
meoh-h2o-9-1          methanol        h2o        0.8008   0.1992
acetone-h2o-1-1       propanone       h2o        0.1962   0.8038
acetone-h2o-95-5      propanone       h2o        0.8226   0.1774
acetone-h2o-98-2      propanone       h2o        0.9228   0.0772
acn-h2o-9-1           acetonitrile    h2o        0.7569   0.2431
